        "### 3.1 Loss Functions\n",
        "\n",
        "The Pix2PixHD model combines multiple loss terms to train the generator:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Generator Losses**\n",
        "- **G_GAN** (GAN adversarial loss) encourages generated images to fool the multi-scale discriminator\n",
        "- **G_GAN_Feat** (GAN feature matching loss) matches intermediate features between real and fake images in the discriminator\n",
        "- **G_VGG** (VGG perceptual loss) is a feature matching loss based on VGG19 pretrained on ImageNet\n",
        "\n",
        "**VGG Perceptual Loss (G_VGG)**\n",
        "VGG is used **only for loss computation**, not as a generator or discriminator. The implementation uses **VGG19** pretrained on ImageNet, extracting features at 5 depths:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Layer | Output | Weight |\n",
        "|-------|--------|--------|\n",
        "| relu1_1 | 64 channels | 1/32 |\n",
        "| relu2_1 | 128 channels | 1/16 |\n",
        "| relu3_1 | 256 channels | 1/8 |\n",
        "| relu4_1 | 512 channels | 1/4 |\n",
        "| relu5_1 | 512 channels | 1.0 |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Loss formula:**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$L_{VGG} = \\lambda_{feat} \\times \\sum_{i=1}^{5} w_i \\cdot L1\\left(VGG_{fake}^i, VGG_{real}^i.detach()\\right)$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Where:\n",
        "- $w_i$ = layer weights [1/32, 1/16, 1/8, 1/4, 1.0]\n",
        "- $\\lambda_{feat} = 10.0$ (scaling factor)\n",
        "- Real image features are **detached** to prevent gradient flow through VGG\n",
        "\n",
        "Is interesting to mention that the $VGG_{real}^i.detach()$ operation is crucial to ensure that the VGG network is not updated during training and that the gradients only flow through the generator parameters when computing `loss_G.backward()`. This allows the generator to learn to produce images that match the perceptual features of the real images without affecting the pretrained VGG weights.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Discriminator Losses**\n",
        "- **D_real** Real image classification loss\n",
        "- **D_fake** Fake (generated) image classification loss\n",
        "\n",
        "The total generator loss is: `loss_G = G_GAN + G_GAN_Feat + G_VGG`\n",
        "The total discriminator loss is: `loss_D = D_real + D_fake`\n"
      ]
    },
